# src/backend — composition root and domain modules.

This package holds the application. See
[docs/architecture/backend.md](../../docs/architecture/backend.md) for the layer
and module rules `docs/architecture/backend.verify.mjs` enforces.

```
src/backend/                 # git mv this when the project renames it; update backend_root
  app/
    main.py                  # composition root: builds and wires the app
    core/                    # cross-cutting, no domain knowledge
    modules/
      <domain>/              # router, schemas, service, repository, ...
    workers/                 # process that drains this module's tasks
  tests/                     # mirrors app/modules; testpaths in pyproject.toml
```

`app/modules/orders/` is a reference module: a `router → service → repository`
chain that exists so `boundary-check` has something to verify on day one.
Replace it with the first real domain rather than growing it.
